# SYNOPSIS

```usage
logname
```

# DESCRIPTION

`logname` prints the user's login name, as the C library's `getlogin` gives it, followed by a newline.
That is the environment variable `LOGNAME`.
It takes no arguments.
It is sbase's command, in `/boot/bin/posix`: the POSIX namespace (a manifest's `ns=posix`, made by `/lib/ns/posix`, see namespace(6)) binds that directory before `/boot/bin` on `/bin`, so a POSIX program finds it there.

# SEE ALSO

whoami(1), users(6), svc(6); sbase's page is `third_party/sbase/logname.1` in the repository

# DIAGNOSTICS

With no login name `logname` says `logname: no login name` and exits 1.
An argument prints the usage message and exits 1.

# BUGS

Nothing on VectraOS sets `LOGNAME`, so `logname` fails unless the environment it was given has it, as a manifest's `env=` can (see svc(6)).
The name is not checked against the users file.
